# `sink int` (#38, Liz: "do 1 plus a"): what a floor or a conversion to an
# integer reads may move by one unit, as the user allows: |v' - v| <= 1
# moves floor and truncation by at most one, so the integer is the
# reference's or a neighbour.  A floor is read through to its argument,
# converted or stored; an unsigned conversion takes a little less than
# one (below -1 it would be undefined); a compare takes nothing.
#
# without the word: the conversion is a root with no budget
simplify float c in [0, 1] nofile
```glsl
int Lvl(float c) { return int(floor(exp2(c * 0.5) * 16.0)); }
```
# with it: exp2 as a degree-1 polynomial (0.143 of the unit)
simplify float c in [0, 1] sink int nofile
```glsl
int Lvl(float c) { return int(floor(exp2(c * 0.5) * 16.0)); }
```
# an unsigned conversion, and a floor stored as a float
simplify float c in [0, 1] sink int nofile
```glsl
uint Lvl(float c) { return uint(exp2(c * 0.5) * 16.0); }
```
simplify float c in [0, 1] sink int nofile
```glsl
float Lvl(float c) { return floor(exp2(c * 0.5) * 16.0); }
```
# a compare takes no budget, whatever the word
simplify float c in [0, 1] sink int nofile
```glsl
int Lvl(float c) { return exp2(c * 0.5) * 16.0 > 20.0 ? 1 : 0; }
```
# in English
simplify c in [0, 1], the integer may be off by one, nofile
```glsl
int Lvl(float c) { return int(floor(exp2(c * 0.5) * 16.0)); }
```
# with a format too: the conversion takes the unit, the returned value
# the format's step
simplify float c in [0, 1] sink unorm8 sink int nofile
```glsl
float Lvl(float c, out int k) { k = int(exp2(c * 0.5) * 16.0); return exp2(c * 0.5) * 0.25; }
```
# a word that is neither a format nor int
simplify float sink int2 nofile
```glsl
int Lvl(float c) { return int(c * 3.0); }
```
